## 2. Methodology and Data Sources

This report is generated automatically from a T-Pot HIVE honeypot deployment
consisting of Cowrie (SSH/Telnet), Dionaea (SMB/malware), Heralding (credential
capture), Snare/Tanner (web attacks), Honeytrap (arbitrary TCP), and FATT
(fingerprinting) sensors. Attack telemetry is indexed in an internal Elasticsearch
instance and queried via the Analyser pipeline. Session-level events are
classified against:

- **MITRE ATT&CK** — for attacker technique identification
- **Lockheed Martin Cyber Kill Chain** — for attack stage classification
- **NIST Cybersecurity Framework** — for recommendation structuring

Narrative interpretation is provided by a locally-hosted large language model
(llama3.2:3b via Ollama). No cloud LLM services are invoked; all raw log data
remains on the analyst workstation.

